*.egg-info/
runs/
demo/
history/*.bak
!history/README.md

# Versioned predecessors: they stay on disk but do not go into the public
# repository. An adversarial review demonstrated on 2026-09-08 that three of
# four history/*.bak files were tracked -- history/README.md claimed the
# opposite -- and that plugin/herdr-plugin.toml.v2026-* carries an absolute
# home path in an EXECUTABLE line. `git rm --cached` takes them out of the
# delivery without removing them; the content stays in the history.
*.bak
plugin/*.v2026-*
plugin/bin/hoh-latest-de
policy/*.txt.v*

# Build output. Measured 2026-09-08: 18 files under build/lib/ were tracked --
# a stale copy of the source, including an older policy file. Adding the rule
# does not untrack them (see history/README.md for the same lesson); the
# exclusion from the public repository happens in D8 via the export's path
# selection.
build/
